---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site';

const mail = `mailto:${site.email}`;
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy policy | Kuriova"
  heading="Privacy"
  description="What kuriova.com and Kuriova's tools collect: no cookies, no accounts, cookie-free analytics, and read-only access to our own YouTube channels."
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> kuriova.com sets no cookies, has no accounts and no forms, and does not sell or
    share personal information. This page explains the little that is collected and why.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Kuriova makes documentaries and publishes them on channels such as Kuriova Science. In this policy “Kuriova”, “we”
    and “us” mean Kuriova. Questions go to <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and measure page speed. It uses no
      cookies, no local storage and no fingerprinting, and it reports totals such as page views, referring sites,
      countries and browser types. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is hosted by Vercel, which processes technical request data, such as IP address
      and browser type, to deliver the pages and protect them from abuse. See <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy">Vercel’s privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Video thumbnails.</strong> Thumbnails of our latest videos load from YouTube’s image servers, which receive
      your IP address as part of the request. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    If you write to <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>, we use your name, address and message only to reply and to handle
    what you asked about, such as a sponsorship or licensing request. We keep the conversation for as long as it is
    useful for that purpose and for our business records, and we delete it on request unless the law requires us to
    keep it.
  </p>

  <h2>Our channels on other platforms</h2>
  <p>
    When you watch, follow or comment on Kuriova on YouTube, Instagram, TikTok, Facebook or X, that platform’s own
    privacy policy applies. We see only what those platforms show every channel owner, such as public comments and
    total audience figures.
  </p>

  <h2>Kuriova Ops and Google user data</h2>
  <p>
    Kuriova Ops is our internal tool for reporting on Kuriova’s own YouTube channels. It is used only by Kuriova, and it
    connects only to Google accounts that Kuriova owns. It does not access the Google account of any viewer or other
    person.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What it accesses.</strong> Through the YouTube Data API, YouTube Analytics API and YouTube Reporting API,
      with read-only permissions, it reads our own channels’ public video details and their analytics reports, such as
      views, watch time, audience retention and subscriber counts. Analytics reports are aggregated and do not identify
      individual viewers.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How it uses the data.</strong> Only to measure how our videos perform and to decide what to make next.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Storage.</strong> Access tokens and report data are stored on Kuriova’s own server, with tokens kept in
      encrypted form. Report data is kept while it is useful for comparing our videos over time.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sharing.</strong> We do not sell Google user data, share it with third parties, use it for advertising, or
      use it to develop, improve or train general-purpose AI or machine-learning models.
    </li>
    <li>
      Kuriova Ops’ use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
      including the Limited Use requirements.
    </li>
    <li>
      Kuriova Ops uses YouTube API Services. By using it you agree to the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms">YouTube Terms of Service</a>, and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a> applies. Access can be revoked at any time
      from the <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google security settings page</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask what personal information we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it, by writing to <a href={mail}>{site.email}</a>. We reply within one month.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, we update this page and the date at the top.
  </p>
</Prose>
